584
00:23:45,040 --> 00:23:46,120
Angel?

585
00:23:46,120 --> 00:23:47,000
This one.

586
00:23:47,280 --> 00:23:47,720
Really?

587
00:23:47,720 --> 00:23:49,280
♪I've always had a pair♪

588
00:23:49,280 --> 00:23:50,040
♪Of invisible...♪

589
00:23:50,040 --> 00:23:50,960
(Isn't that it?)

590
00:23:50,960 --> 00:23:51,840
Not that one.

591
00:23:51,840 --> 00:23:52,640
Then what is it?

592
00:23:54,120 --> 00:23:55,640
What's that song called?

593
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:57,960
♪In that fairy tale♪

594
00:23:57,960 --> 00:23:59,840
(Sings passionately)
♪You have to believe♪

595
00:24:01,320 --> 00:24:01,960
That one.

596
00:24:01,960 --> 00:24:03,680
♪In that fairy tale♪

597
00:24:03,680 --> 00:24:04,680
♪You have to believe♪

598
00:24:05,480 --> 00:24:05,800
Fairy Tale.

599
00:24:05,800 --> 00:24:07,200
Let's pick Fairy Tale, then.

600
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:09,280
♪I wanna be♪

601
00:24:09,280 --> 00:24:10,600
(Starts singing instantly)
♪The angel♪

602
00:24:10,600 --> 00:24:13,720
♪You love in fairy tales♪

603
00:24:13,720 --> 00:24:16,200
♪I'll spread my arms♪

604
00:24:16,200 --> 00:24:19,960
♪Into wings to protect you♪

605
00:24:19,960 --> 00:24:22,120
♪I wanna be♪

606
00:24:22,120 --> 00:24:23,800
(Improvising)
♪The angel♪

607
00:24:23,800 --> 00:24:27,000
♪You love in fairy tales♪

608
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:29,640
(Lost in the music)
♪I'll spread my arms♪

609
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:30,440
♪Into wings to protect you♪

610
00:24:30,440 --> 00:24:31,680
He even changed the key.

611
00:24:31,680 --> 00:24:32,320
(Laughs)

612
00:24:32,320 --> 00:24:33,400
He changed the key.

613
00:24:34,120 --> 00:24:39,720
(Lost in the song)
♪With a happy ending♪

614
00:24:39,720 --> 00:24:40,400
Nice.

615
00:24:41,320 --> 00:24:41,800
Great.

616
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:42,440
Not bad, right?

617
00:24:42,440 --> 00:24:43,540
(Happy)

618
00:24:45,640 --> 00:24:46,880
Let's find one.

619
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:48,200
A Thousand and One Nights.

620
00:24:48,200 --> 00:24:49,960
999 Roses.

621
00:24:49,960 --> 00:24:51,480
I won't sing my best song.

622
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:53,240
Come on, sing it.

623
00:24:53,240 --> 00:24:53,640
Nah, I...

624
00:24:53,640 --> 00:24:54,440
This song...

625
00:24:54,440 --> 00:24:55,080
I'm

626
00:24:55,080 --> 00:24:55,720
really good at it.

627
00:24:55,720 --> 00:24:57,040
It's my secret weapon.

628
00:24:57,680 --> 00:24:58,520
This one...

629
00:24:58,520 --> 00:24:59,300
Alright, I'll sing it.

630
00:24:59,300 --> 00:25:00,060
(Time to show off)

631
00:25:00,600 --> 00:25:01,400
I'm in a good mood today.

632
00:25:01,560 --> 00:25:02,480
I'll bring out my secret weapon.

633
00:25:02,880 --> 00:25:04,000
Gotta bring out the best.

634
00:25:05,200 --> 00:25:08,720
(#KaraokeKingModeActivated)
♪I've already planted for you♪

635
00:25:08,720 --> 00:25:11,520
♪999 roses♪

636
00:25:12,120 --> 00:25:12,520
Nice!

637
00:25:12,520 --> 00:25:15,360
♪My heart has no regrets♪

638
00:25:15,360 --> 00:25:18,160
♪Every fold is for you♪

639
00:25:18,160 --> 00:25:22,760
♪I left home to save my beloved Li♪

640
00:25:22,760 --> 00:25:26,560
♪Who knew I'd top the imperial exam?♪

641
00:25:26,560 --> 00:25:28,320
♪Let's face the world together♪

642
00:25:28,320 --> 00:25:30,160
♪And live wild and free♪

643
00:25:30,160 --> 00:25:32,760
♪I'll never forget you♪

644
00:25:33,360 --> 00:25:34,760
He's singing
with his brows furrowed.

645
00:25:34,760 --> 00:25:35,200
No idea why.

646
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:36,300
Am I singing with feeling?

647
00:25:36,300 --> 00:25:37,000
(Hopeful)

648
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:39,880
Yeah, you've got tons of soul.

649
00:25:42,480 --> 00:25:44,200
Then where's my applause?

650
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:45,160
I don't hear any.

651
00:25:45,680 --> 00:25:46,480
Sounds great!

652
00:25:49,680 --> 00:25:51,160
Amazing! So much soul!

653
00:25:51,160 --> 00:25:52,280
You sang so well!

654
00:25:53,440 --> 00:25:54,040
Sounds a bit fake.

655
00:25:54,920 --> 00:25:55,720
What?

656
00:25:56,160 --> 00:25:57,120
Sounds a bit fake.

657
00:25:58,000 --> 00:25:58,760
What's fake?

658
00:26:01,400 --> 00:26:02,800
What else do you wanna sing, sir?

659
00:26:02,800 --> 00:26:04,660
(Go ahead)
Am I the only one singing?

660
00:26:04,680 --> 00:26:05,800
How about...

661
00:26:06,560 --> 00:26:07,320
Sailor works too.

662
00:26:07,320 --> 00:26:07,680
Sailor?

663
00:26:07,960 --> 00:26:08,480
Sailor.

664
00:26:08,480 --> 00:26:09,320
We all know that one.

665
00:26:11,240 --> 00:26:12,940
(Tianjin's walking jukebox)
I know way too many songs.

666
00:26:13,120 --> 00:26:14,640
I can't even think of one now.

667
00:26:14,640 --> 00:26:15,600
Too many.

668
00:26:15,960 --> 00:26:16,680
You know them all.

669
00:26:18,880 --> 00:26:19,960
Showdown.

670
00:26:21,880 --> 00:26:22,960
Let's take turns singing verses.

671
00:26:22,960 --> 00:26:23,540
(Invites him to duet)

672
00:26:25,400 --> 00:26:26,080
Sure.

673
00:26:26,080 --> 00:26:26,940
(Takes it with both hands)

674
00:26:29,040 --> 00:26:30,780
You sing the first verse.

675
00:26:30,780 --> 00:26:31,260
(Yiheng starts)

676
00:26:31,760 --> 00:26:32,200
Okay.

677
00:26:32,680 --> 00:26:33,160
I'll take the second.

678
00:26:33,160 --> 00:26:33,760
Okay.

679
00:26:33,760 --> 00:26:34,300
(Hahaha)

680
00:26:42,400 --> 00:26:44,120
♪The bitter sand♪

681
00:26:44,120 --> 00:26:46,480
♪Stings my face as it blows♪

682
00:26:46,880 --> 00:26:48,800
(He's got talent)
♪Like my father's scolding♪

683
00:26:48,800 --> 00:26:49,880
♪My mother's tears♪

684
00:26:49,880 --> 00:26:51,440
♪I'll never forget♪

685
00:26:52,060 --> 00:26:53,260
(Exchanges a look)

686
00:26:55,440 --> 00:26:56,560
My dad holds grudges.

687
00:26:56,880 --> 00:26:57,720
If you sing better than him,

688
00:26:57,720 --> 00:26:59,360
he'll put you in his blacklist.

689
00:27:00,560 --> 00:27:03,120
♪I like being alone by the sea♪

690
00:27:03,120 --> 00:27:05,040
♪Rolling up my pants♪

691
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:06,200
♪With bare feet♪

692
00:27:06,200 --> 00:27:08,000
♪Walking on the sand♪

693
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:10,400
♪He said, through the storms♪

694
00:27:10,400 --> 00:27:12,640
♪What's a little pain?♪

695
00:27:12,640 --> 00:27:14,840
♪Wipe your tears, don't be afraid♪

696
00:27:14,840 --> 00:27:15,440
Having fun?

697
00:27:15,440 --> 00:27:17,800
♪At least we still have dreams♪

698
00:27:17,800 --> 00:27:20,440
♪He said, through the storms♪

699
00:27:20,440 --> 00:27:22,760
♪What's a little pain?♪

700
00:27:22,760 --> 00:27:24,240
♪Wipe your tears♪

701
00:27:24,240 --> 00:27:25,160
♪Don't ask♪

702
00:27:25,160 --> 00:27:27,760
♪Why♪

703
00:27:29,520 --> 00:27:30,320
Brilliant!

704
00:27:31,020 --> 00:27:31,480
(Happy)

705
00:27:31,480 --> 00:27:32,000
Sounds great.

706
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:32,840
100 points!

707
00:27:33,860 --> 00:27:34,700
(Smiles)

708
00:27:35,120 --> 00:27:36,520
Don't you two know this song?

709
00:27:36,720 --> 00:27:37,400
I do.

710
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:38,080
He knows it.

711
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:39,920
Let's sing together.

712
00:27:39,920 --> 00:27:40,720
Okay.

713
00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:44,840
♪Snow begins to fall in my world♪

714
00:27:44,840 --> 00:27:47,360
♪Too cold to love another day♪

715
00:27:47,360 --> 00:27:50,640
♪A loving husband and wife♪

716
00:27:50,640 --> 00:27:53,440
♪Even hardship feels sweet♪

717
00:27:53,440 --> 00:27:55,760
Well sung!

718
00:27:55,760 --> 00:27:57,080
Do I always hold the mic like this?

719
00:27:57,560 --> 00:27:58,320
Like a rapper.

720
00:27:58,320 --> 00:27:59,080
I hold it like that too.

721
00:27:59,080 --> 00:27:59,960
You do too?

722
00:28:01,560 --> 00:28:05,040
♪There's a time to meet and part♪

723
00:28:05,040 --> 00:28:05,840
Nice!

724
00:28:08,040 --> 00:28:10,280
♪How could I bear to see you♪

725
00:28:10,280 --> 00:28:11,680
♪Suffer?♪

726
00:28:11,680 --> 00:28:14,800
♪Miles of azaleas never fade♪

727
00:28:20,940 --> 00:28:24,220
(Beijing, Xing and Si's birthday)

728
00:28:25,360 --> 00:28:26,520
Let's go find the sisters.

729
00:28:26,520 --> 00:28:27,240
Let's go!

730
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:29,520
See if they're ready.

731
00:28:31,680 --> 00:28:33,360
- Are you guys ready?
- What's up?

732
00:28:33,960 --> 00:28:35,600
Pretty much.

733
00:28:35,760 --> 00:28:36,440
We're ready.

734
00:28:36,440 --> 00:28:37,880
Ready to go anytime, right?

735
00:28:38,280 --> 00:28:39,720
We'll let you know when we arrive.

736
00:28:39,880 --> 00:28:40,560
Okay.

737
00:28:40,560 --> 00:28:41,560
Alright, bye.

738
00:28:42,840 --> 00:28:44,080
After your last amusement park trip,

739
00:28:44,080 --> 00:28:45,040
do you wanna go again?

740
00:28:45,640 --> 00:28:47,600
Actually, I wouldn't mind.

741
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:48,960
What did you two miss last time?

742
00:28:49,960 --> 00:28:50,840
We missed Silent Hill.

743
00:28:51,200 --> 00:28:54,000
(Teaming up)
Then the four of us can try it.

744
00:28:54,360 --> 00:28:56,240
The haunted house you two missed.

745
00:28:58,480 --> 00:28:59,240
Wait.

746
00:28:59,640 --> 00:29:00,360
(Tank: leads the way)
I'll be the tank.

747
00:29:00,360 --> 00:29:01,120
You can be the tank.

748
00:29:01,120 --> 00:29:02,200
(Expression changes instantly)
I can do that. No problem.

749
00:29:02,200 --> 00:29:03,840
Those two aren't afraid of heights.

750
00:29:04,240 --> 00:29:05,040
They love thrill rides.

751
00:29:05,040 --> 00:29:06,240
But they're easily scared.

752
00:29:06,240 --> 00:29:07,400
She's braver than me, though.

753
00:29:07,400 --> 00:29:09,040
(The biggest scaredy-cat)
Even she's braver than me.

754
00:29:09,040 --> 00:29:11,040
(Don't even start)
Don't even get me started on you.

755
00:29:11,040 --> 00:29:12,160
You're a total scaredy-cat.

756
00:29:12,240 --> 00:29:13,000
I don't know why.

757
00:29:13,000 --> 00:29:14,240
(Didn't see that coming)
I thought I was pretty brave.

758
00:29:14,240 --> 00:29:15,200
The storm's passed,

759
00:29:15,200 --> 00:29:16,680
and now you think you're tough again?

760
00:29:17,480 --> 00:29:18,440
All talk.

761
00:29:20,200 --> 00:29:22,120
You know what's funny?

762
00:29:22,120 --> 00:29:23,680
Those two sisters,

763
00:29:23,680 --> 00:29:25,000
they're actually around our age.

764
00:29:25,390 --> 00:29:26,240
About 25 or 26.

765
00:29:26,240 --> 00:29:28,080
But I feel like

766
00:29:28,080 --> 00:29:29,520
they're still like little kids.

767
00:29:29,960 --> 00:29:30,920
Actually, between us,

768
00:29:30,920 --> 00:29:32,440
I'm younger than Si.

769
00:29:32,440 --> 00:29:33,640
And you're older than Xing.

770
00:29:33,640 --> 00:29:34,400
Yeah.

771
00:29:34,400 --> 00:29:35,680
So you're really the brother-in-law.

772
00:29:35,680 --> 00:29:36,760
A proper brother-in-law.

773
00:29:36,940 --> 00:29:38,860
(Keep talking. I like it)

774
00:29:39,120 --> 00:29:40,120
Even though Si's older than me,

775
00:29:40,120 --> 00:29:41,320
I feel like

776
00:29:41,600 --> 00:29:42,840
the way she acts

777
00:29:42,840 --> 00:29:44,400
doesn't make her seem older.

778
00:29:46,040 --> 00:29:46,880
We're here.

779
00:29:48,680 --> 00:29:49,480
Xing,

780
00:29:49,920 --> 00:29:51,960
we're downstairs now.

781
00:29:52,560 --> 00:29:54,000
Come down whenever you're ready.

782
00:29:54,320 --> 00:29:55,120
Okay.

783
00:29:55,700 --> 00:29:57,780
(Exit)

784
00:29:58,720 --> 00:29:59,920
We've got so many bags.

785
00:29:59,920 --> 00:30:00,630
Yeah.

786
00:30:00,880 --> 00:30:02,240
Can you see them?

787
00:30:02,240 --> 00:30:03,120
Yeah, I see them!

788
00:30:03,720 --> 00:30:05,160
(Goes to greet them)
Look at all those bags.

789
00:30:05,160 --> 00:30:07,040
We packed quite a few outfits.

790
00:30:07,740 --> 00:30:09,700
(Gets the bouquets ready)

791
00:30:10,280 --> 00:30:11,800
Here, give me your bags.

792
00:30:11,800 --> 00:30:12,600
I'll put them in the trunk.

793
00:30:12,600 --> 00:30:12,880
Okay.

794
00:30:12,880 --> 00:30:14,320
You can keep the small bags.

795
00:30:14,320 --> 00:30:14,900
Sure.

796
00:30:14,900 --> 00:30:16,540
(Keeping an eye out)

797
00:30:17,720 --> 00:30:19,200
Wait, leave it inside for now.

798
00:30:19,200 --> 00:30:19,540
Carry it out.

799
00:30:19,540 --> 00:30:20,260
(Plotting in plain sight)
Carry it out.

800
00:30:20,260 --> 00:30:20,760
Hold it later.

801
00:30:20,760 --> 00:30:21,480
Okay.

802
00:30:22,300 --> 00:30:23,700
(Notices)

803
00:30:24,780 --> 00:30:25,760
(Senses something's up)

804
00:30:25,760 --> 00:30:26,920
What are those two doing?

805
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:32,840
Why are you two acting so shady?

806
00:30:33,180 --> 00:30:35,020
(Don't say anything)

807
00:30:35,280 --> 00:30:36,520
He won't let him say anything.

808
00:30:36,520 --> 00:30:37,880
No, look at those two.

809
00:30:39,080 --> 00:30:40,400
(Si's POV)
They're acting so sneaky!

810
00:30:40,400 --> 00:30:41,160
What's going on?

811
00:30:43,160 --> 00:30:44,120
Hey, Si,

812
00:30:44,120 --> 00:30:44,920
happy birthday.

813
00:30:45,520 --> 00:30:46,320
Thank you.

814
00:30:46,800 --> 00:30:48,120
Happy birthday, babe.

815
00:30:48,560 --> 00:30:49,360
Thank you.

816
00:30:49,880 --> 00:30:51,080
Look at this little Star Guy.

817
00:30:51,080 --> 00:30:52,680
Star Guy.

818
00:30:52,680 --> 00:30:53,660
(Starry-eyed)

819
00:30:53,960 --> 00:30:54,840
A little bunny.

820
00:30:54,840 --> 00:30:56,240
In Mid-Autumn Festival colors.

821
00:30:56,240 --> 00:30:57,280
It's so cute!

822
00:30:57,440 --> 00:30:58,240
Little flowers.

823
00:30:58,680 --> 00:30:59,480
Thank you.

824
00:31:00,020 --> 00:31:00,700
(Shy)

825
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:01,720
So cute.

826
00:31:04,200 --> 00:31:05,680
You look beautiful today.

827
00:31:05,680 --> 00:31:07,030
(Adoringly)
It even matches my outfit.

828
00:31:07,040 --> 00:31:08,760
It goes really well
with your outfit too.

829
00:31:08,760 --> 00:31:09,320
Really?

830
00:31:09,320 --> 00:31:10,440
Yeah. Here, hold this.

831
00:31:10,440 --> 00:31:11,160
I'll take your picture.

832
00:31:12,560 --> 00:31:15,440
Wait, why's Si taking your picture?

833
00:31:15,440 --> 00:31:16,480
It's your birthday?

834
00:31:17,080 --> 00:31:18,720
Yeah, why'd you
suddenly start taking mine?

835
00:31:19,000 --> 00:31:19,800
So random.

836
00:31:21,120 --> 00:31:21,560
How about this?

837
00:31:21,560 --> 00:31:22,760
I'll take one of you sisters together.

838
00:31:22,760 --> 00:31:24,080
Our first photo together today.

839
00:31:24,080 --> 00:31:24,880
Come on.

840
00:31:26,080 --> 00:31:27,920
You two look gorgeous.

841
00:31:30,200 --> 00:31:30,960
Hop in.

842
00:31:37,120 --> 00:31:38,840
Let's go!

843
00:31:39,760 --> 00:31:41,400
It's such a beautiful sunny day.

844
00:31:41,400 --> 00:31:43,560
Even the weather's
perfect for your birthday.

845
00:31:46,480 --> 00:31:48,200
Isn't that because you two are here?

846
00:31:48,200 --> 00:31:49,400
Can't argue with that.

847
00:31:49,500 --> 00:31:50,660
(Holds on tight)

848
00:31:50,760 --> 00:31:52,600
You two look really handsome today.

849
00:31:53,080 --> 00:31:54,480
Only today?

850
00:31:54,480 --> 00:31:55,480
We're always...

851
00:31:55,480 --> 00:31:56,600
Yeah, always handsome.

852
00:31:56,600 --> 00:31:57,680
Just extra handsome today.

853
00:31:58,200 --> 00:31:59,000
(Shy)
Not bad.

854
00:31:59,440 --> 00:32:00,920
(Xing's POV)
Where are we going now?

855
00:32:01,440 --> 00:32:04,160
We're going to an indoor amusement park!

856
00:32:05,320 --> 00:32:07,280
Haven't you two always wanted to go?

857
00:32:07,760 --> 00:32:08,840
(Xing's POV)
Are you excited, babe?

858
00:32:08,840 --> 00:32:09,480
Yeah.

859
00:32:09,480 --> 00:32:10,640
What about Si and Yihang?

860
00:32:10,640 --> 00:32:12,240
I'm excited. Are you?

861
00:32:12,240 --> 00:32:13,160
(Si's POV)
I'm super excited.

862
00:32:13,160 --> 00:32:13,560
Really?

863
00:32:13,560 --> 00:32:14,520
Yeah, I'm so excited.

864
00:32:14,520 --> 00:32:17,160
What are you most excited to try today?

865
00:32:17,160 --> 00:32:18,500
(Xing's POV)
I really like trampolines.

866
00:32:18,500 --> 00:32:19,060
(Trampolines)
Trampolines?

867
00:32:19,060 --> 00:32:20,000
There's basketball too.

868
00:32:20,010 --> 00:32:21,400
(Indoor basketball)
We can shoot some hoops.

869
00:32:21,400 --> 00:32:23,440
I'll show you some real skills.

870
00:32:23,440 --> 00:32:24,140
(Domain expansion)

871
00:32:24,280 --> 00:32:25,000
It's trampoline basketball.

872
00:32:25,000 --> 00:32:26,080
I'll help you dunk.

873
00:32:26,320 --> 00:32:27,760
They have trampoline basketball too?

874
00:32:27,760 --> 00:32:28,440
Yeah.

875
00:32:28,440 --> 00:32:30,200
You're the king of trampolines

876
00:32:30,200 --> 00:32:31,120
and the king of basketball.

877
00:32:31,120 --> 00:32:33,040
What happens when you combine both?

878
00:32:33,360 --> 00:32:34,040
Yeah, I'll just

879
00:32:34,040 --> 00:32:36,200
(Getting fired up)
jump 15 meters into the air

880
00:32:36,200 --> 00:32:36,960
and straight into the hoop.

881
00:32:36,960 --> 00:32:38,320
Can't wait to see that.

882
00:32:38,560 --> 00:32:39,440
Sure, no problem.

883
00:32:39,600 --> 00:32:40,960
When I was little, I'd bounce so high

884
00:32:40,960 --> 00:32:42,480
I'd land on someone else's shoulders.

885
00:32:42,480 --> 00:32:43,800
Right on their neck.

886
00:32:43,800 --> 00:32:46,280
Well, you haven't seen what we can do.

887
00:32:46,280 --> 00:32:47,000
You two?

888
00:32:47,640 --> 00:32:49,200
There's this trampoline trick

889
00:32:49,200 --> 00:32:50,760
where you can bounce up to the ceiling

890
00:32:50,760 --> 00:32:51,720
and walk right up the wall.

891
00:32:51,720 --> 00:32:52,640
You know that one?

892
00:32:52,640 --> 00:32:53,840
We can walk right up.

893
00:32:53,840 --> 00:32:54,680
I can.

894
00:32:54,680 --> 00:32:55,160
You can?

895
00:32:55,160 --> 00:32:55,960
I really can.

896
00:32:56,440 --> 00:32:58,400
Can you do a backflip on a trampoline?

897
00:32:58,400 --> 00:32:59,960
I can show you later.

898
00:32:59,960 --> 00:33:00,980
(Another pro?)
Sure.

899
00:33:01,280 --> 00:33:02,280
On our way here,

900
00:33:02,280 --> 00:33:03,680
Yihang and I were talking.

901
00:33:03,800 --> 00:33:04,880
Last time, they

902
00:33:04,880 --> 00:33:06,840
went to that escape room
with five themes, right?

903
00:33:07,360 --> 00:33:08,320
They only tried three.

904
00:33:08,320 --> 00:33:11,080
I said the four of us should...

905
00:33:11,360 --> 00:33:12,080
Try the other two together.

906
00:33:12,080 --> 00:33:12,520
Yeah.

907
00:33:12,520 --> 00:33:14,160
When you went last time,

908
00:33:14,160 --> 00:33:15,120
were you scared?

909
00:33:15,120 --> 00:33:16,440
He nearly fell over in there.

910
00:33:16,440 --> 00:33:17,460
(Calls him out)

911
00:33:17,520 --> 00:33:18,640
He was that scared?

912
00:33:18,640 --> 00:33:19,960
Yeah. And in there,

913
00:33:20,240 --> 00:33:22,520
he wasn't even screaming normally.

914
00:33:22,520 --> 00:33:23,640
His screams

915
00:33:23,640 --> 00:33:25,000
blended right in with the ghosts'.

916
00:33:25,000 --> 00:33:25,640
(Have some mercy)

917
00:33:25,640 --> 00:33:27,200
I couldn't tell where they came from.

918
00:33:27,200 --> 00:33:28,360
They were coming from everywhere.

919
00:33:28,360 --> 00:33:29,720
Turns out it was him.

920
00:33:29,720 --> 00:33:30,640
Every time I turned a corner...

921
00:33:32,600 --> 00:33:34,400
That's the sound he'd make!

922
00:33:34,400 --> 00:33:35,400
And because of that,

923
00:33:35,400 --> 00:33:36,720
I couldn't tell if it was a ghost or...

924
00:33:36,720 --> 00:33:39,280
I'd get scared and go, oh!

925
00:33:39,440 --> 00:33:40,440
I didn't know I made that noise.

926
00:33:40,440 --> 00:33:42,160
I only realized afterward.

927
00:33:42,160 --> 00:33:43,680
(Even more excited now)
Alright, let's go together next time.

928
00:33:44,800 --> 00:33:45,960
Look at his face.

929
00:33:46,320 --> 00:33:47,240
He's a little scared.

930
00:33:47,960 --> 00:33:49,080
We're almost there.

931
00:33:49,080 --> 00:33:50,280
That was pretty quick.

932
00:33:51,560 --> 00:33:52,920
We're here! Let's go!

933
00:33:52,920 --> 00:33:53,720
Let's go!

934
00:33:55,560 --> 00:33:56,520
Hello!

935
00:33:56,520 --> 00:33:57,080
Hi!

936
00:33:57,080 --> 00:33:57,920
Hello!

937
00:33:59,520 --> 00:34:00,720
This place is huge, right?

938
00:34:01,760 --> 00:34:02,900
It's pretty nice.

939
00:34:03,160 --> 00:34:04,360
This is awesome.

940
00:34:06,040 --> 00:34:07,080
This spot...

941
00:34:07,080 --> 00:34:08,600
This looks really fun.

942
00:34:08,920 --> 00:34:10,040
This looks cool.

943
00:34:10,280 --> 00:34:10,960
You and Yihang,

944
00:34:10,960 --> 00:34:11,880
jump together!

945
00:34:12,320 --> 00:34:13,720
You two sisters show us how.

946
00:34:18,080 --> 00:34:19,480
Why's watching people bounce so funny?

947
00:34:21,140 --> 00:34:22,200
(Can't stop laughing)

948
00:34:22,200 --> 00:34:23,320
They look like little action figures.

949
00:34:24,640 --> 00:34:26,360
You two jump. Bounce him up.

950
00:34:27,220 --> 00:34:29,760
(Jumps right in)
Come on, let's hold hands too!

951
00:34:36,900 --> 00:34:38,780
(Nonstop bouncing)

952
00:34:47,120 --> 00:34:48,940
I think I've figured this out.

953
00:34:48,940 --> 00:34:50,900
(You sure?)

954
00:34:51,240 --> 00:34:51,800
I've got it.

955
00:34:51,800 --> 00:34:52,520
I know how.

956
00:34:52,520 --> 00:34:53,600
Three, two, one, run.

957
00:34:56,700 --> 00:34:58,580
(Watching closely)

958
00:34:59,740 --> 00:35:00,620
(Perfect takeoff)

959
00:35:05,180 --> 00:35:06,580
(Front flip (failed attempt))

960
00:35:10,180 --> 00:35:10,750
Oh my God.

961
00:35:11,140 --> 00:35:12,980
(Everyone cracks up)

962
00:35:16,960 --> 00:35:18,060
Those two are kinda clumsy.

963
00:35:18,060 --> 00:35:18,700
(Time for a little roast)

964
00:35:18,780 --> 00:35:20,940
(Too embarrassed to show his face)

965
00:35:22,360 --> 00:35:23,920
You two try it.

966
00:35:24,720 --> 00:35:26,120
Not sure we can jump across.

967
00:35:28,280 --> 00:35:29,800
Then just run across,

968
00:35:29,800 --> 00:35:30,640
right?

969
00:35:30,640 --> 00:35:31,700
(Genius move)

970
00:35:32,600 --> 00:35:33,600
Are you out shopping?

971
00:35:34,280 --> 00:35:35,520
Taking a stroll, babe?

972
00:35:42,640 --> 00:35:43,360
Let's try this one.

973
00:35:43,920 --> 00:35:44,760
This one again?

974
00:35:45,600 --> 00:35:47,040
Come on, babe. Try it.

975
00:35:47,520 --> 00:35:48,840
Maybe we need to jump together.

976
00:35:48,840 --> 00:35:49,640
Come on, jump.

977
00:36:00,420 --> 00:36:02,180
(Still learning)

978
00:36:02,200 --> 00:36:03,280
Look how he bounces her up.

979
00:36:06,820 --> 00:36:07,540
(Got it)

980
00:36:07,540 --> 00:36:08,360
Let's see if I can bounce you off.

981
00:36:08,360 --> 00:36:09,280
Okay.

982
00:36:10,980 --> 00:36:12,580
(Gets bounced off instead)

983
00:36:14,780 --> 00:36:16,820
(Takes a direct hit)

984
00:36:18,760 --> 00:36:20,960
Took a knee to the face.

985
00:36:21,100 --> 00:36:22,780
(Struggles to move)

986
00:36:25,480 --> 00:36:27,960
Did I hit you?

987
00:36:29,080 --> 00:36:29,920
Let me see.

988
00:36:30,060 --> 00:36:31,200
(Already red)

989
00:36:31,200 --> 00:36:31,720
Here?

990
00:36:31,720 --> 00:36:32,520
Yeah.

991
00:36:34,080 --> 00:36:35,840
You look like a bee-stung puppy!

992
00:36:36,480 --> 00:36:37,080
Really?

993
00:36:37,600 --> 00:36:38,240
Why did you bump your face

994
00:36:38,240 --> 00:36:39,760
(Teasing)
into her knee?

995
00:36:39,900 --> 00:36:41,620
(Who does that?)

996
00:36:41,760 --> 00:36:43,040
Does it hurt? Let me see.

997
00:36:43,040 --> 00:36:43,800
It's okay.

998
00:36:43,800 --> 00:36:44,600
It's a little red.

999
00:36:45,160 --> 00:36:46,440
Feels a little warm.

1000
00:36:46,440 --> 00:36:47,320
It really is warm.

1001
00:36:50,800 --> 00:36:51,520
Wanna head out?

1002
00:36:51,880 --> 00:36:52,280
Let's go.

1003
00:36:54,240 --> 00:36:55,280
There's basketball.

1004
00:36:55,800 --> 00:36:57,160
You and Yihang can shoot some hoops.

1005
00:36:57,360 --> 00:36:57,880
Let's see.

1006
00:36:57,880 --> 00:36:58,880
Get a running start.

1007
00:36:58,880 --> 00:36:59,680
You try.

1008
00:37:00,360 --> 00:37:01,720
Let's sit here and watch them.

1009
00:37:02,060 --> 00:37:03,260
(Getting serious)

1010
00:37:05,260 --> 00:37:06,540
(Goes for a huge layup)

1011
00:37:06,580 --> 00:37:08,180
(Watching closely)

1012
00:37:13,300 --> 00:37:15,100
(Can't hold back the laughter)

1013
00:37:16,200 --> 00:37:17,400
Take it slow. No rush.

1014
00:37:21,760 --> 00:37:22,920
No, you need to get closer.

1015
00:37:22,920 --> 00:37:24,720
(Advice from the Dunk King)
It's hard to control otherwise.

1016
00:37:24,720 --> 00:37:26,020
(Save my reputation)
Come on.

1017
00:37:33,700 --> 00:37:35,060
(An epic rim grab)

1018
00:37:38,120 --> 00:37:39,840
Don't rip their hoop off.

1019
00:37:40,040 --> 00:37:41,000
This is tricky.

1020
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:41,700
(It's gotta be the ball's fault)

1021
00:37:41,740 --> 00:37:43,780
(#IntenseBasketballSession)

1022
00:37:43,780 --> 00:37:44,740
(Loses his grip)

1023
00:37:54,040 --> 00:37:55,480
Stop laughing!

1024
00:37:55,960 --> 00:37:57,080
You scared the hoop.

1025
00:37:58,120 --> 00:37:59,480
Let's try something else.

1026
00:38:00,540 --> 00:38:02,980
(Practice some more first)

1027
00:38:03,240 --> 00:38:04,520
Let's split up for now.

1028
00:38:04,640 --> 00:38:05,920
Sure, let's go.

1029
00:38:06,120 --> 00:38:07,520
Look at this bike.

1030
00:38:08,480 --> 00:38:09,400
(360-degree spinning bike)
It spins all the way around.

1031
00:38:09,400 --> 00:38:10,040
Try it.

1032
00:38:13,820 --> 00:38:15,220
(Excited)

1033
00:38:15,740 --> 00:38:16,460
(Woohoo)

1034
00:38:18,940 --> 00:38:21,140
(Yihang's POV)

1035
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:22,480
Your turn.

1036
00:38:25,060 --> 00:38:26,740
(Scared)

1037
00:38:27,560 --> 00:38:28,200
I'm done.

1038
00:38:28,520 --> 00:38:30,200
What's wrong? Got scared?

1039
00:38:35,040 --> 00:38:36,120
(Impressed)
You're so good!

1040
00:38:36,120 --> 00:38:37,200
Here, you shoot.

1041
00:38:37,600 --> 00:38:38,240
For girls,

1042
00:38:38,240 --> 00:38:38,840
if you shoot like this,

1043
00:38:38,840 --> 00:38:40,560
(Sharing tips)
you'll be more accurate.

1044
00:38:41,060 --> 00:38:41,980
(Technique unlocked)

1045
00:38:45,320 --> 00:38:46,080
You're so good.

1046
00:38:46,480 --> 00:38:47,640
I learned from the best.

1047
00:38:47,640 --> 00:38:50,860
(Learned from the best)

1048
00:38:52,680 --> 00:38:53,640
Nice shot.

1049
00:38:54,260 --> 00:38:55,240
(The two can't
get enough of trampolines)

1050
00:38:55,240 --> 00:38:56,880
Come on. Three, two, one, together.

1051
00:39:00,540 --> 00:39:02,180
(Playful attack)

1052
00:39:02,600 --> 00:39:03,560
You're so annoying!

1053
00:39:11,020 --> 00:39:12,980
(Helps her up)

1054
00:39:14,540 --> 00:39:16,340
(An adorable warning)

1055
00:39:16,480 --> 00:39:18,160
You just lost your balance.

1056
00:39:23,720 --> 00:39:25,400
I'm not playing with you!

1057
00:39:25,760 --> 00:39:26,960
I'm done playing with you!

1058
00:39:27,720 --> 00:39:29,000
Sit down and let me bounce you up.

1059
00:39:29,400 --> 00:39:30,120
I'll sit.

1060
00:39:30,120 --> 00:39:31,060
(Plays along)

1061
00:39:31,480 --> 00:39:32,040
Okay.

1062
00:39:35,560 --> 00:39:36,600
How's this?

1063
00:39:36,840 --> 00:39:37,960
You look like a bouncing monkey.

1064
00:39:39,480 --> 00:39:40,760
Did you fly up?

1065
00:39:41,160 --> 00:39:41,840
You sit here. Let me try.

1066
00:39:41,840 --> 00:39:43,080
See if I can bounce you up.

1067
00:39:44,780 --> 00:39:46,420
(Liftoff)

1068
00:39:49,160 --> 00:39:50,600
Dare to cross the balance beam?

1069
00:39:50,600 --> 00:39:51,400
I do.

1070
00:39:51,640 --> 00:39:52,780
(Cautious)
You do?

1071
00:39:52,800 --> 00:39:53,600
Of course.

1072
00:39:54,220 --> 00:39:56,580
(Brave Xing)

1073
00:39:57,360 --> 00:39:58,800
Not bad, lad.

1074
00:40:01,320 --> 00:40:02,480
I'm grabbing coins.

1075
00:40:02,880 --> 00:40:04,320
You're stealing my eggs!

1076
00:40:06,120 --> 00:40:07,560
You took them all.

1077
00:40:09,120 --> 00:40:10,400
(Interactive ball battle)
We can play the four-player one.

1078
00:40:10,400 --> 00:40:11,600
How does this work?

1079
00:40:12,880 --> 00:40:14,040
You attack, and I defend.

1080
00:40:14,040 --> 00:40:14,480
Okay.

1081
00:40:16,620 --> 00:40:18,460
(Stepping over the line when throwing)

1082
00:40:25,600 --> 00:40:27,800
You two, move back a little.

1083
00:40:27,800 --> 00:40:29,440
Xing came over here

1084
00:40:29,440 --> 00:40:30,240
and did this.

1085
00:40:34,000 --> 00:40:34,800
Babe,

1086
00:40:35,400 --> 00:40:36,720
you're not scoring a single point.

1087
00:40:37,200 --> 00:40:37,960
Pretty good, huh?

1088
00:40:37,960 --> 00:40:38,520
That's impressive.

1089
00:40:39,560 --> 00:40:41,600
I think this is how we should do it.

1090
00:40:41,600 --> 00:40:43,120
He's already on his knees.

1091
00:40:44,200 --> 00:40:45,360
I've figured out the trick.

1092
00:40:47,360 --> 00:40:48,400
You're pretty good.

1093
00:40:48,960 --> 00:40:49,520
Am I good?

1094
00:40:49,520 --> 00:40:50,760
Amazing. You're seriously good.

1095
00:40:53,120 --> 00:40:54,920
Look at those two.
Their poses are hilarious.

1096
00:40:55,840 --> 00:40:57,840
Look at them.

1097
00:41:07,680 --> 00:41:08,640
Let's go eat.

1098
00:41:08,640 --> 00:41:09,360
This place is fun.

1099
00:41:09,360 --> 00:41:10,120
It really is.

1100
00:41:13,280 --> 00:41:15,040
I can already smell the barbecue.

1101
00:41:15,040 --> 00:41:16,720
The barbecue smell is so strong.

1102
00:41:16,720 --> 00:41:17,040
Let's go.

1103
00:41:21,420 --> 00:41:22,660
(Northeast-style barbecue)

1104
00:41:23,640 --> 00:41:24,480
Like this.

1105
00:41:25,160 --> 00:41:25,640
Let's go.

1106
00:41:27,000 --> 00:41:27,880
How do you like it?

1107
00:41:28,120 --> 00:41:29,160
Pretty good.

1108
00:41:33,200 --> 00:41:34,000
Have you had

1109
00:41:34,000 --> 00:41:34,880
Northeast-style barbecue before, Yihang?

1110
00:41:34,880 --> 00:41:36,160
No, I haven't.

1111
00:41:36,880 --> 00:41:37,840
Never tried it?

1112
00:41:38,440 --> 00:41:39,400
It's really my first time.

1113
00:41:39,410 --> 00:41:40,930
(First taste of Northeast-style barbecue)
I've really never had it before.

1114
00:41:40,960 --> 00:41:42,600
Do you like lamb chop skewers?

1115
00:41:42,600 --> 00:41:43,880
Yeah.

1116
00:41:43,880 --> 00:41:45,120
(Placing the order)
Let's get all the fresh lamb.

1117
00:41:45,320 --> 00:41:46,760
I love beef skewers
and fatty pork skewers.

1118
00:41:46,760 --> 00:41:47,960
Medium spicy.

1119
00:41:48,600 --> 00:41:49,320
Lamb chop skewers.

1120
00:41:49,320 --> 00:41:50,400
You can't eat lamb.

1121
00:41:50,400 --> 00:41:52,320
Get some air-dried
fatty pork skewers for yourself.

1122
00:41:52,640 --> 00:41:53,040
That works.

1123
00:41:53,040 --> 00:41:54,360
You two order what you want,

1124
00:41:54,360 --> 00:41:55,440
and we'll order ours so we don't

1125
00:41:55,440 --> 00:41:56,160
get duplicates.

1126
00:41:57,240 --> 00:41:57,960
Right.

1127
00:41:58,360 --> 00:41:59,120
Do you want this?

1128
00:41:59,720 --> 00:42:01,200
I feel like you'd like it.

1129
00:42:01,200 --> 00:42:01,880
That's okay.

1130
00:42:02,760 --> 00:42:03,720
(Beef skewers +1)
Let's get some beef skewers.

1131
00:42:03,720 --> 00:42:04,000
Okay.

1132
00:42:04,000 --> 00:42:05,420
I'm good with bell pepper beef skewers.

1133
00:42:05,420 --> 00:42:05,720
(Bell pepper beef skewers +1)

1134
00:42:05,720 --> 00:42:06,080
Okay.

1135
00:42:06,200 --> 00:42:06,990
(Chicken tendon skewers +1)
Chicken tendon skewers.

1136
00:42:07,000 --> 00:42:08,100
The thick pork tendon skewers
should be nice and chewy.

1137
00:42:08,100 --> 00:42:08,700
(Thick pork tendon skewers +1)

1138
00:42:08,760 --> 00:42:09,660
Let's get a slice of bread too.

1139
00:42:09,660 --> 00:42:10,180
(Bread slice +1)

1140
00:42:11,040 --> 00:42:12,320
(Juicy Korean sausage +1)
Juicy Korean sausage.

1141
00:42:12,480 --> 00:42:13,200
(Oven-roasted pork belly +1)
Oven-roasted pork belly.

1142
00:42:13,240 --> 00:42:13,960
(Spicy chicken +1)
Let's get some spicy chicken.

1143
00:42:14,040 --> 00:42:14,760
(Grilled mushrooms +1)
Grilled mushrooms.

1144
00:42:14,920 --> 00:42:15,560
(Classic mala hot pot +1)
Classic mala hot pot.

1145
00:42:15,560 --> 00:42:16,120
(Beef tendon +1)
Beef tendon.

1146
00:42:16,320 --> 00:42:17,240
