Thank you.

1424
00:52:23,080 --> 00:52:24,720
Let's cut the cake.

1425
00:52:25,200 --> 00:52:25,920
So let's just dig in

1426
00:52:25,920 --> 00:52:27,760
and eat as much cake as we want, oaky?

1427
00:52:27,760 --> 00:52:28,160
Okay.

1428
00:52:28,160 --> 00:52:30,120
Yes. Take a bite.

1429
00:52:30,120 --> 00:52:30,920
Let's have a toast.

1430
00:52:31,600 --> 00:52:33,360
Here. Happy birthday.

1431
00:52:33,720 --> 00:52:34,280
Xing and Siying,

1432
00:52:34,280 --> 00:52:35,200
happy birthday.

1433
00:52:38,720 --> 00:52:39,640
This is delicious.

1434
00:52:40,480 --> 00:52:41,960
What will happen

1435
00:52:41,960 --> 00:52:43,360
if I smeared the frosting on your face?

1436
00:52:44,200 --> 00:52:45,400
You're so dead.

1437
00:52:45,400 --> 00:52:46,240
I'm dead.

1438
00:52:49,600 --> 00:52:50,040
I was reminded

1439
00:52:50,040 --> 00:52:51,440
of the day with the elephants.

1440
00:52:51,680 --> 00:52:53,280
You smeared mud all over my face.

1441
00:52:54,720 --> 00:52:55,520
When it's your birthday,

1442
00:52:55,520 --> 00:52:57,120
your face is going
to be covered in frosting.

1443
00:52:57,120 --> 00:52:57,880
(Covered in frosting)

1444
00:52:57,880 --> 00:52:58,680
How's that?

1445
00:52:59,280 --> 00:52:59,880
I...

1446
00:52:59,880 --> 00:53:01,320
Can we ask to get involved too?

1447
00:53:01,520 --> 00:53:02,270
(Nods)
Sure.

1448
00:53:02,280 --> 00:53:02,680
Yes.

1449
00:53:02,680 --> 00:53:03,480
Can we?

1450
00:53:03,480 --> 00:53:04,360
Yes.

1451
00:53:04,960 --> 00:53:05,920
Sure. No problem.

1452
00:53:05,920 --> 00:53:08,980
(The youngest of the family)

1453
00:53:10,840 --> 00:53:12,200
Siying, do you

1454
00:53:12,200 --> 00:53:13,040
and Yihang ever get

1455
00:53:13,040 --> 00:53:14,320
into little arguments like this?

1456
00:53:15,080 --> 00:53:15,840
Sometimes.

1457
00:53:15,840 --> 00:53:17,440
Actually, we do.

1458
00:53:20,240 --> 00:53:21,480
There was this one time at a park.

1459
00:53:21,480 --> 00:53:22,400
We had a bit of a disagreement.

1460
00:53:22,400 --> 00:53:22,960
So we sat

1461
00:53:22,960 --> 00:53:24,400
on the bench.

1462
00:53:24,400 --> 00:53:25,840
He said his piece,

1463
00:53:25,840 --> 00:53:26,920
and I said mine.

1464
00:53:26,920 --> 00:53:28,320
We went back and forth until 2AM.

1465
00:53:29,520 --> 00:53:31,720
But from what I've seen of you two.

1466
00:53:31,720 --> 00:53:32,840
We're not like you.

1467
00:53:32,840 --> 00:53:34,440
You two go at each other without stopping.

1468
00:53:35,720 --> 00:53:37,320
When he's worked up,

1469
00:53:37,320 --> 00:53:38,680
he talks really fast.

1470
00:53:39,360 --> 00:53:40,520
She would think I'm being too much,

1471
00:53:40,520 --> 00:53:42,440
but I'm just speaking a little quicker.

1472
00:53:43,200 --> 00:53:43,920
You know.

1473
00:53:43,920 --> 00:53:44,600
His voice

1474
00:53:44,600 --> 00:53:46,760
isn't exactly...

1475
00:53:46,760 --> 00:53:47,520
Both our voices

1476
00:53:47,520 --> 00:53:48,520
are pretty soft,

1477
00:53:48,520 --> 00:53:49,200
and sometimes unclear.

1478
00:53:49,200 --> 00:53:50,360
And with the speed,

1479
00:53:50,360 --> 00:53:52,800
we sound like a machine that won't stop.

1480
00:53:52,800 --> 00:53:54,280
We both have a lot to say.

1481
00:53:54,280 --> 00:53:55,680
We just want to get it all out
to each other.

1482
00:53:58,640 --> 00:53:59,800
From what I remember,

1483
00:53:59,800 --> 00:54:02,240
every time we have

1484
00:54:02,240 --> 00:54:03,640
a little argument

1485
00:54:03,640 --> 00:54:05,080
or some minor disagreement,

1486
00:54:05,080 --> 00:54:05,860
we actually become closer after.

1487
00:54:05,860 --> 00:54:06,880
(Understand each other better
over time)

1488
00:54:06,880 --> 00:54:08,360
So it's getting better.

1489
00:54:08,360 --> 00:54:09,000
Yeah.

1490
00:54:09,600 --> 00:54:11,600
I think it's a good thing.

1491
00:54:11,600 --> 00:54:12,560
It's a good thing.

1492
00:54:12,560 --> 00:54:13,720
This way, I can better

1493
00:54:13,720 --> 00:54:15,720
understand where the conflict is.

1494
00:54:16,040 --> 00:54:17,280
So through things like this,

1495
00:54:17,280 --> 00:54:18,720
I will understand

1496
00:54:18,720 --> 00:54:20,000
and tolerate him better.

1497
00:54:20,760 --> 00:54:22,000
Understand and tolerate him better.

1498
00:54:22,000 --> 00:54:22,840
Right. When we run

1499
00:54:22,840 --> 00:54:23,840
into similar problems again,

1500
00:54:23,840 --> 00:54:24,440
we already

1501
00:54:24,440 --> 00:54:26,160
sort of

1502
00:54:26,160 --> 00:54:27,040
know each other better.

1503
00:54:27,040 --> 00:54:27,880
We know what to do.

1504
00:54:27,880 --> 00:54:28,800
Our past experiences

1505
00:54:29,360 --> 00:54:31,880
helps us understand each other better.

1506
00:54:31,880 --> 00:54:33,360
It's only when emotions run high

1507
00:54:33,360 --> 00:54:33,920
that she would say

1508
00:54:33,920 --> 00:54:35,840
what's really on her mind.

1509
00:54:39,400 --> 00:54:41,200
When you two have

1510
00:54:41,200 --> 00:54:43,360
little arguments,

1511
00:54:43,360 --> 00:54:45,880
do you tell Xing?

1512
00:54:46,080 --> 00:54:46,640
Yes.

1513
00:54:46,640 --> 00:54:46,920
Yeah.

1514
00:54:46,920 --> 00:54:47,440
Twice.

1515
00:54:47,680 --> 00:54:48,840
She was very fair.

1516
00:54:48,840 --> 00:54:49,720
(Fair)
Xing was really fair.

1517
00:54:49,720 --> 00:54:50,280
Super fair.

1518
00:54:50,280 --> 00:54:51,120
She embodies it.

1519
00:54:51,120 --> 00:54:53,100
(She serves justice)

1520
00:54:53,200 --> 00:54:54,400
You defined what "fair" is.

1521
00:54:55,160 --> 00:54:57,760
But I think if Si

1522
00:54:57,760 --> 00:54:58,920
heard you out

1523
00:54:58,920 --> 00:55:00,240
about something similar,

1524
00:55:00,240 --> 00:55:01,040
she'd be just as fair.

1525
00:55:01,040 --> 00:55:02,860
(She serves justice too)
Si is also very fair.

1526
00:55:03,040 --> 00:55:04,240
But we don't do that.

1527
00:55:04,240 --> 00:55:06,240
We've never argued.

1528
00:55:07,280 --> 00:55:08,400
Get along perfectly.

1529
00:55:08,680 --> 00:55:10,480
Sometimes,

1530
00:55:10,480 --> 00:55:12,080
I might get angry.

1531
00:55:12,080 --> 00:55:14,280
But you're just so calm and collected,

1532
00:55:14,280 --> 00:55:16,000
and speaking so reasonably.

1533
00:55:16,000 --> 00:55:17,360
I just can't stay mad.

1534
00:55:19,920 --> 00:55:22,800
Everyone will have

1535
00:55:23,440 --> 00:55:25,000
their little mood swings.

1536
00:55:25,960 --> 00:55:27,520
But we never really

1537
00:55:27,520 --> 00:55:28,520
say...

1538
00:55:28,960 --> 00:55:31,040
Blow up at each other.

1539
00:55:31,040 --> 00:55:32,200
Whenever I'm feeling

1540
00:55:32,200 --> 00:55:34,040
a little off,

1541
00:55:34,040 --> 00:55:35,760
she's always like...

1542
00:55:36,360 --> 00:55:37,200
Well.

1543
00:55:37,200 --> 00:55:38,240
She'll comfort me.

1544
00:55:39,120 --> 00:55:40,280
And when she's upset,

1545
00:55:40,280 --> 00:55:41,760
I'll try to comfort her too.

1546
00:55:41,760 --> 00:55:42,640
It's never a case

1547
00:55:42,640 --> 00:55:44,720
of both of us losing our tempers
at once.

1548
00:55:44,720 --> 00:55:45,520
Never.

1549
00:55:49,360 --> 00:55:49,920
Right?

1550
00:55:49,920 --> 00:55:50,760
That's true.

1551
00:55:50,760 --> 00:55:51,760
That's it.

1552
00:55:52,180 --> 00:55:54,700
(Smiles)

1553
00:55:55,160 --> 00:55:56,520
Do we have disposable aprons?

1554
00:55:57,400 --> 00:55:58,240
We do.

1555
00:55:59,520 --> 00:56:00,280
Do we?

1556
00:56:02,000 --> 00:56:02,680
Put one on.

1557
00:56:02,680 --> 00:56:03,120
I'm worried

1558
00:56:03,120 --> 00:56:04,000
the oil will splash on you.

1559
00:56:04,460 --> 00:56:06,660
(Helps her put it on)

1560
00:56:09,920 --> 00:56:10,880
Is your head big?

1561
00:56:10,880 --> 00:56:11,400
I'll do it.

1562
00:56:11,400 --> 00:56:11,960
Do you want one?

1563
00:56:12,520 --> 00:56:13,040
Okay.

1564
00:56:13,040 --> 00:56:14,040
Just drape it over yourself.

1565
00:56:14,640 --> 00:56:15,200
Like this.

1566
00:56:15,200 --> 00:56:16,160
Cover your legs.

1567
00:56:17,760 --> 00:56:19,000
How is this birthday different

1568
00:56:19,000 --> 00:56:20,480
from the ones you've had before?

1569
00:56:20,480 --> 00:56:22,000
It's livelier this year.

1570
00:56:24,320 --> 00:56:25,200
We've got two more people here.

1571
00:56:25,440 --> 00:56:27,520
Usually, it's just the two of us alone.

1572
00:56:27,920 --> 00:56:29,880
But it's so fun being here
with you guys.

1573
00:56:37,600 --> 00:56:38,800
How do you celebrate usually, Yihang?

1574
00:56:39,560 --> 00:56:40,960
When I was little,

1575
00:56:40,960 --> 00:56:41,920
there would be a crowd.

1576
00:56:41,920 --> 00:56:43,280
The whole family would get together.

1577
00:56:43,280 --> 00:56:43,720
Yes.

1578
00:56:43,720 --> 00:56:45,240
My mom would make me

1579
00:56:45,240 --> 00:56:46,400
homemade noodles.

1580
00:56:46,400 --> 00:56:47,360
Like one really long noodle.

1581
00:56:48,200 --> 00:56:49,280
One unbroken strand.

1582
00:56:49,280 --> 00:56:49,760
Yes.

1583
00:56:49,760 --> 00:56:51,000
And my sister would make a cake.

1584
00:56:51,800 --> 00:56:53,160
That must feel so cozy.

1585
00:56:53,160 --> 00:56:53,880
Yeah. As time went by,

1586
00:56:53,880 --> 00:56:55,360
I realized that birthdays

1587
00:56:55,360 --> 00:56:57,280
would only feel that way at home.

1588
00:56:58,800 --> 00:56:59,880
Home is where you are.

1589
00:56:59,880 --> 00:57:01,940
(Home is where you are)

1590
00:57:03,080 --> 00:57:05,680
I knew he was going to say that.

1591
00:57:08,120 --> 00:57:09,760
You know Yihang much better now.

1592
00:57:09,760 --> 00:57:11,280
Well yeah. Wherever you two are.

1593
00:57:11,280 --> 00:57:12,520
I guess that's really how it is

1594
00:57:12,520 --> 00:57:13,400
for Yihang and me.

1595
00:57:18,360 --> 00:57:19,680
Shall we leave?

1596
00:57:19,960 --> 00:57:20,680
Sure. Let's go.

1597
00:57:20,680 --> 00:57:21,480
Okay.

1598
00:57:23,560 --> 00:57:25,600
When we get back,
I'll put the massage chair together.

1599
00:57:25,600 --> 00:57:26,760
You can lie down for a bit.

1600
00:57:26,760 --> 00:57:27,320
Put it together?

1601
00:57:27,880 --> 00:57:28,680
Is it here already?

1602
00:57:28,840 --> 00:57:29,960
The massage chair's here.

1603
00:57:31,720 --> 00:57:32,360
Hello.

1604
00:57:32,360 --> 00:57:33,600
It's the massage chair.

1605
00:57:33,920 --> 00:57:36,680
Can you deliver in the afternoon?

1606
00:57:37,040 --> 00:57:39,080
Don't send it over now.

1607
00:57:39,080 --> 00:57:40,320
(Confirms present delivery time)

1608
00:57:40,320 --> 00:57:41,400
Hello.

1609
00:57:43,680 --> 00:57:45,120
Yes.

1610
00:57:45,600 --> 00:57:46,920
Your delivery is reaching.

1611
00:57:46,920 --> 00:57:49,400
Leave it against the wall
to the right of the door.

1612
00:57:49,400 --> 00:57:50,240
Sure.

1613
00:57:50,240 --> 00:57:52,280
(Confirms delivery time too)
Sure. Thank you.

1614
00:57:53,040 --> 00:57:54,600
This is great. We can both use it now.

1615
00:57:56,560 --> 00:57:58,440
Honestly, everything we bought

1616
00:57:58,440 --> 00:57:59,280
is for you two to share.

1617
00:57:59,280 --> 00:58:00,360
It's for sharing.

1618
00:58:00,540 --> 00:58:01,860
(Smiles)

1619
00:58:02,480 --> 00:58:03,360
Come on. Let's...

1620
00:58:03,360 --> 00:58:04,040
Let's go.

1621
00:58:04,040 --> 00:58:04,920
go home.

1622
00:58:05,520 --> 00:58:06,320
Come.

1623
00:58:09,360 --> 00:58:10,280
Is this the bike?

1624
00:58:10,280 --> 00:58:11,360
Yup. That's the bike.

1625
00:58:12,020 --> 00:58:13,360
(Cui Yihang's gift: A bike)

1626
00:58:13,360 --> 00:58:14,320
This is the massage chair.

1627
00:58:15,320 --> 00:58:16,280
It's so huge.

1628
00:58:16,500 --> 00:58:18,440
(Huge birthday present)

1629
00:58:18,440 --> 00:58:20,640
Now you can get a massage
at home every day.

1630
00:58:23,280 --> 00:58:26,720
Babe, where do you want to put it?

1631
00:58:26,960 --> 00:58:28,200
The massage chair?

1632
00:58:28,720 --> 00:58:29,800
Let's put it over there.

1633
00:58:29,800 --> 00:58:31,000
How about that spot?

1634
00:58:31,160 --> 00:58:31,960
Sure.

1635
00:58:32,600 --> 00:58:34,040
This is the coffee machine.

1636
00:58:34,540 --> 00:58:36,160
(Cui Yihang's gift: A coffee machine)

1637
00:58:36,160 --> 00:58:36,720
Yihang,

1638
00:58:37,080 --> 00:58:38,280
come here for a second.

1639
00:58:39,240 --> 00:58:39,760
Coming.

1640
00:58:39,760 --> 00:58:40,400
(Moves quickly)

1641
00:58:40,400 --> 00:58:41,280
Okay. Come on.

1642
00:58:41,480 --> 00:58:43,280
(Exerting effort)
One, two, three, lift.

1643
00:58:44,240 --> 00:58:45,480
This is massive.

1644
00:58:46,480 --> 00:58:48,640
You two look like little mascots
standing by the door.

1645
00:58:48,640 --> 00:58:49,560
(Mascots)

1646
00:58:49,560 --> 00:58:50,880
Watch you two unpack it.

1647
00:58:52,720 --> 00:58:53,080
Yes.

1648
00:58:53,080 --> 00:58:54,400
This is the cake

1649
00:58:54,400 --> 00:58:55,560
Meng sent to you two.

1650
00:58:55,900 --> 00:58:57,880
(Sun Qimeng sends a cake)
Let's unbox the cake.

1651
00:58:58,240 --> 00:58:59,040
Sure.

1652
00:59:00,960 --> 00:59:02,320
Look at the little bow.

1653
00:59:08,040 --> 00:59:08,440
Okay.

1654
00:59:08,440 --> 00:59:09,360
We got it right now.

1655
00:59:10,360 --> 00:59:11,240
One, two, three.

1656
00:59:11,580 --> 00:59:12,700
(All muscles working)
Lift.

1657
00:59:14,280 --> 00:59:14,800
Come on.

1658
00:59:15,200 --> 00:59:16,800
Let's carry it over there in one go.

1659
00:59:18,400 --> 00:59:19,360
It's too big.

1660
00:59:19,880 --> 00:59:20,600
Are you tired?

1661
00:59:20,600 --> 00:59:21,320
No.

1662
00:59:22,360 --> 00:59:22,880
Are you tired?

1663
00:59:22,880 --> 00:59:23,680
I'm okay.

1664
00:59:24,680 --> 00:59:25,640
In the mornings,

1665
00:59:25,640 --> 00:59:26,960
we don't see each other when we get up.

1666
00:59:26,960 --> 00:59:27,760
Whoever wakes up first

1667
00:59:27,760 --> 00:59:29,040
(A morning essential)
can come here for a massage.

1668
00:59:29,040 --> 00:59:29,480
Sounds good.

1669
00:59:29,720 --> 00:59:31,040
I'll unbox the coffee machine.

1670
00:59:32,680 --> 00:59:33,600
I think you can

1671
00:59:33,600 --> 00:59:34,480
have coffee every day.

1672
00:59:34,480 --> 00:59:35,520
Yes. That's the good life.

1673
00:59:39,040 --> 00:59:40,200
I think it adjusts

1674
00:59:40,200 --> 00:59:41,400
to each person's body shape.

1675
00:59:41,400 --> 00:59:42,200
It has

1676
00:59:42,680 --> 00:59:44,000
a memory setting.

1677
00:59:44,000 --> 00:59:45,340
(Testing it out)

1678
00:59:45,560 --> 00:59:47,360
Do you know what this chair
reminds me of?

1679
00:59:47,840 --> 00:59:48,800
What does this remind me of?

1680
00:59:48,800 --> 00:59:49,760
The Signal House.

1681
00:59:49,760 --> 00:59:50,140
Yup.

1682
00:59:50,140 --> 00:59:50,980
(Recalls Signal House)

1683
00:59:51,800 --> 00:59:53,600
Let's go downstairs
and try out the bike.

1684
00:59:53,960 --> 00:59:54,940
(Tries out the mountain bike)
Sure.

1685
00:59:55,200 --> 00:59:56,000
Let's go.

1686
00:59:56,800 --> 00:59:57,840
Next time you message me,

1687
00:59:57,840 --> 00:59:59,280
you won't get ahold of me anymore.

1688
00:59:59,280 --> 01:00:00,440
Because you'll fall asleep here.

1689
01:00:01,320 --> 01:00:01,880
I'll try it for you

1690
01:00:01,880 --> 01:00:03,360
and adjust the settings first.

1691
01:00:03,780 --> 01:00:07,060
(Helps her set it up)

1692
01:00:07,320 --> 01:00:08,680
It's pretty light.

1693
01:00:08,680 --> 01:00:09,160
Hop on.

1694
01:00:09,160 --> 01:00:09,920
Let me try.

1695
01:00:12,760 --> 01:00:13,720
This makes it go faster.

1696
01:00:13,720 --> 01:00:14,520
This slows it down.

1697
01:00:14,520 --> 01:00:15,280
Okay. The slower it is

1698
01:00:15,280 --> 01:00:16,480
the easier it is to pedal.

1699
01:00:16,720 --> 01:00:17,720
Try it without changing it first.

1700
01:00:17,720 --> 01:00:18,600
Just give it a go.

1701
01:00:18,600 --> 01:00:19,140
Slowly.

1702
01:00:19,140 --> 01:00:19,940
(Holds her)

1703
01:00:20,600 --> 01:00:21,640
Careful.

1704
01:00:23,920 --> 01:00:25,280
Yes. Slowly.

1705
01:00:31,220 --> 01:00:33,500
(Follows)

1706
01:00:36,540 --> 01:00:38,540
(Smiles)

1707
01:00:41,680 --> 01:00:42,680
Try going faster.

1708
01:00:42,680 --> 01:00:44,080
Go around there.

1709
01:00:44,080 --> 01:00:44,960
Can I go faster?

1710
01:00:44,960 --> 01:00:45,920
You can.

1711
01:00:45,920 --> 01:00:46,440
I'll try it then.

1712
01:00:46,440 --> 01:00:47,640
You can try it.

1713
01:00:52,280 --> 01:00:53,120
I'm speeding up.

1714
01:00:54,520 --> 01:00:55,080
Go on.

1715
01:00:57,900 --> 01:00:59,580
(Happy)

1716
01:00:59,860 --> 01:01:01,340
(Takes photos for the memories)

1717
01:01:09,800 --> 01:01:10,840
Hi.

1718
01:01:16,640 --> 01:01:17,480
You look good.

1719
01:01:21,500 --> 01:01:23,020
(Next episode: Weekend Crush Gathering)

1720
01:01:23,280 --> 01:01:23,880
Hello!

1721
01:01:23,880 --> 01:01:24,520
Hello.

1722
01:01:24,520 --> 01:01:25,680
Hello, Yu Yang.

1723
01:01:26,040 --> 01:01:26,880
Hi.

1724
01:01:26,880 --> 01:01:28,640
Why is there a pot over there?

1725
01:01:28,640 --> 01:01:29,920
It's for something.

1726
01:01:29,920 --> 01:01:31,880
Welcome to Chaos Kitchen.

1727
01:01:31,880 --> 01:01:33,080
(Unique welcome ritual)

1728
01:01:33,080 --> 01:01:34,640
This sound is the funniest.

1729
01:01:34,920 --> 01:01:35,640
Hi.

1730
01:01:35,760 --> 01:01:36,800
I see you met her dad.

1731
01:01:36,800 --> 01:01:37,240
Yeah.

1732
01:01:37,240 --> 01:01:38,200
When did that happen?

1733
01:01:38,440 --> 01:01:39,240
You did quite well.

1734
01:01:39,320 --> 01:01:40,680
How far have things gotten?

1735
01:01:41,360 --> 01:01:42,620
What does your dad think of him?

1736
01:01:42,620 --> 01:01:43,460
(Confidential)

1737
01:01:45,440 --> 01:01:46,360
I really want to cook.

1738
01:01:48,400 --> 01:01:48,920
Are we starting,

1739
01:01:48,920 --> 01:01:49,480
Chef?

1740
01:01:49,680 --> 01:01:50,840
This is so loud.

1741
01:01:51,160 --> 01:01:52,080
Don't you want an apron?

1742
01:01:52,680 --> 01:01:53,480
I do.

1743
01:01:57,040 --> 01:01:57,840
This way.

1744
01:02:00,500 --> 01:02:01,780
(Smoke everywhere)

1745
01:02:02,550 --> 01:02:03,360
Oh my gosh.

1746
01:02:03,360 --> 01:02:04,320
Come over here.

1747
01:02:04,320 --> 01:02:05,440
(Emergency evacuation)
I need to evacuate.

1748
01:02:05,560 --> 01:02:06,160
Yiheng.

1749
01:02:06,160 --> 01:02:07,400
You're using chemical warfare.

1750
01:02:09,600 --> 01:02:10,120
Reunited.

1751
01:02:10,120 --> 01:02:11,240
We're reunited.

1752
01:02:12,760 --> 01:02:13,720
Who brought the yogurt?

1753
01:02:13,760 --> 01:02:15,000
Is there a reason behind it?

1754
01:02:15,200 --> 01:02:15,880
I want everyone's bonds

1755
01:02:15,880 --> 01:02:17,160
to be as thick as yogurt.

1756
01:02:18,880 --> 01:02:20,240
Just like our friendship.

1757
01:02:20,240 --> 01:02:21,400
The more we get together,

1758
01:02:21,400 --> 01:02:22,160
the better it gets.

1759
01:02:22,260 --> 01:02:24,400
(Just like our friendship. The more
we get together, the better it gets.)

1760
01:02:24,400 --> 01:02:25,760
I hope our friendship

1761
01:02:25,760 --> 01:02:28,120
can stay simple and last forever.

1762
01:02:30,560 --> 01:02:31,280
What a line.

1763
01:02:31,320 --> 01:02:32,280
Everyone had a taste.

1764
01:02:32,280 --> 01:02:32,880
A perfect ending.

1765
01:02:46,460 --> 01:02:49,180
♪Morning steam rises
from breakfast stalls♪

1766
01:02:49,180 --> 01:02:51,780
♪Packed subway cars,
barely room to breathe♪

1767
01:02:51,780 --> 01:02:55,980
♪Still half asleep, another day begins♪

1768
01:02:57,140 --> 01:02:59,860
♪The city glows beneath the towers♪

1769
01:02:59,860 --> 01:03:02,500
♪Somewhere beyond the clouds,
a sweet little date awaits♪

1770
01:03:02,500 --> 01:03:06,580
♪But first,
there are endless meetings to survive♪

1771
01:03:07,300 --> 01:03:08,700
♪Even if the fairy tale
only lasts a day♪

1772
01:03:08,700 --> 01:03:10,020
♪I'll still give it everything I have♪

1773
01:03:10,020 --> 01:03:11,340
♪Love out loud♪

1774
01:03:11,340 --> 01:03:12,740
♪Don't let this summer slip away♪

1775
01:03:12,740 --> 01:03:13,980
♪Cupid's arrow is already on its way♪

1776
01:03:13,980 --> 01:03:15,380
♪Don't act like you didn't see it♪

1777
01:03:15,380 --> 01:03:18,340
♪Just be a little braver♪

1778
01:03:18,340 --> 01:03:21,180
♪Keep moving♪

1779
01:03:21,180 --> 01:03:24,540
♪There's a little spark shining
in your eyes♪

1780
01:03:26,900 --> 01:03:29,260
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

1781
01:03:39,700 --> 01:03:42,500
♪Keep moving♪

1782
01:03:42,500 --> 01:03:45,140
♪Life can be complicated,
yet beautifully simple♪

1783
01:03:45,140 --> 01:03:47,780
♪Go discover♪

1784
01:03:47,780 --> 01:03:50,460
♪That heartbeat you've been longing
to let out♪

1785
01:03:50,460 --> 01:03:53,140
♪Come closer♪

1786
01:03:53,140 --> 01:03:56,540
♪There's a little spark shining
in your eyes♪

1787
01:03:58,980 --> 01:04:01,780
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪
